/E (In many countries of the world, religious and political institutions have been the main providers of mass education for children. Their motivation for founding schools has, of course, been to promote their own ideologies and recruit followers. But children at school are vulnerable and impressionable, and therefore need to be protected from having ideologies imposed upon them. Education is fundamentally incompatible with indoctrination and the promotion of particular worldviews. So the education provided in schools should be based on scientific atheism rather than religion or politics. )
